# CODEOWNERS for a service created from this skeleton (Proposed).
# Replace the placeholders with the real GitHub teams from the README ownership
# block (owning_squad), the platform owners and the data-contracts owners, and
# turn on required code-owner review for main.
# Last match wins: keep the waiver rule below every broader rule.

*                            @<org>/<owning-squad>

# Platform guard, once the service vendors it into a chart of its own
# (charts/fintechbankx-service README in fintechbankx-platform-delivery-iac-cicd-templates,
# "Vendoring the guard", step 5): only the platform owners approve a change to
# the vendored file, the verifier, the workflow that pins the digest (rename
# deployability.yml to the file that holds the pin), or this file.
/deploy/helm/*/templates/_fbx_helpers.tpl   @<org>/<platform-owners>
/scripts/ci/verify-vendored-guard.sh        @<org>/<platform-owners>
/.github/workflows/deployability.yml        @<org>/<platform-owners>
/.github/CODEOWNERS                         @<org>/<platform-owners>

# Contract waivers read by contract-checks.yml (OpenAPI and AsyncAPI, any
# directory). Only the data-contracts owners approve a breaking change; the
# provider squad cannot waive its own break.
**/*.accepted-breaking.txt   @<org>/<data-contracts-owners>
